sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant Order as Order<br/>dual-layer
  participant Redis as Redis<br/>hot path
  participant ODB as PostgreSQL<br/>durable

  Note over Order,ODB: Session Creation - Both layers
  Order->>ODB: Create ACTIVE session
  ODB-->>Order: Session persisted
  Order->>Redis: Create session cache<br/>with TTL
  Redis-->>Order: Session cached

  Note over Order,ODB: Cart Update - Redis only
  Order->>Redis: Update cart snapshot
  Redis-->>Order: Cart updated

  Note over Order,ODB: Order Submit - Commit to PostgreSQL
  Order->>Redis: Read cart
  Redis-->>Order: Cart snapshot
  Order->>ODB: Create PENDING order<br/>link to session
  ODB-->>Order: Order committed
  Order->>Redis: Clear cart
  Redis-->>Order: Cart deleted

  Note over Order,ODB: Redis Failure - Recovery
  Order->>Redis: Read session
  Redis--xOrder: Cache miss
  Order->>ODB: Find session by<br/>tenant + table
  ODB-->>Order: Session still ACTIVE
  Order->>Redis: Rebuild cache
  Redis-->>Order: Session restored

  Note over Order,ODB: Redis is hot path. PostgreSQL is durable source of truth for session lifecycle.
